# Local development

This repo uses **Bun** as its package manager/runtime and **Docker** for Postgres.

## Prerequisites

- Bun `1.3.x` (installed to `~/.bun`; ensure `~/.bun/bin` is on `PATH`)
- Docker Desktop running (Postgres container `crm-postgres` on `:5432`)
- Node `>=22`

## First-time setup

```bash
bun install                 # root .env must exist first (db postinstall reads DATABASE_URL)
docker compose up -d        # Postgres on :5432
cp .env.example .env        # fill in the required values (see below)
bun run db:deploy           # apply migrations
bun run db:seed             # optional demo pipeline (idempotent)
bun run dev                 # app :3000, api :3001
```

## Required `.env` values

- `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` — `openssl rand -base64 32`
- `ALLOWED_SIGN_IN` — email domain(s)/address(es) allowed to register or sign in
  (empty = nobody). The whole authorisation model.

`DATABASE_URL` already matches the docker-compose Postgres. Everything else in
`.env.example` is optional; a missing key removes a capability, never throws.

## Auth (this install: email + password)

Sign-in runs on **email + password**; Google OAuth is optional.

- Register/sign in at `/sign-in` with an address on `ALLOWED_SIGN_IN`.
- Google sign-in is hidden unless `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`
  are set (redirect URI `http://localhost:3001/api/auth/callback/google`).
- Differs from upstream — see `docs/local-setup.md` › "Auth changes from
  upstream" for the exact files.

## Common tasks

| Command                              | What it does                          |
| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |
| `bun run dev`                        | Everything, watch mode                |
| `bun run build`                      | Build all apps and packages           |
| `bun run test`                       | Test suite                            |
| `bun run check-types`                | `tsc --noEmit` everywhere             |
| `bun run lint` / `bun run format`    | Biome                                 |
| `bun run db:migrate`                 | Create + apply a migration            |
| `bun run db:studio`                  | Prisma Studio                         |
| `bun run --filter=api dev:session`   | Print a session cookie for a local user |

Scope any task with a Turborepo filter, e.g. `bun run dev --filter=api`.

## Notes

- There is **one `.env`** at the repo root, read by all three processes.
  Never add a per-package `.env`.
- `apps/api/src/generated/server.ts` is committed; `build` must never
  regenerate it. Regenerate locally with `bun run --filter=api trpc:generate`.
